puted the done/open split against disk after the 30-item expansion and found four sorry-free modules still uncovered. `AJC.rr.divisor` now records the Weil-divisor and degree substrate (Picard/DivDegree, Picard/DivFunctorDef); `AJC.cech.pushpull` names Cohomology/CechHigherDirectImage; `AJC.fbc` records that the global flat-base-change scaffolding is sorry-free and that all three open obligations are in CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional.", "created_at": "2026-07-27T00:53:02+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [], "lean": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 0}, {"sha": "64e7bdabbd061d806cd59b738579ffb7034c33a7", "short_sha": "64e7bdabbd", "subject": "build(ajc): drive the import-hygiene campaign wave by wave over the import DAG", "summary": "**Why waves.** A modules minimal-import probe is only correct once its whole transitive project-import closure is umbrella-free: while a dependency still says `import Mathlib` it hands the entire library to the importer, and the `linter.minImports` pass then reports every Mathlib module as redundant. Each wave therefore converts exactly the bare modules whose project dependencies are already clean, rebuilds them so the next waves probes see the narrowed oleans, and repeats. Wave 1 is the 27 DAG sources.", "created_at": "2026-07-27T00:51:05+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/scripts/deumbrella-wave.sh", "category": "other", "add": 79, "del": 0}], "lean": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 1}, {"sha": "ea62cf030168378aae3a869ebfb60f87232b180e", "short_sha": "ea62cf0301", "subject": "build(ajc): add the de-umbrella and budget-trim tooling for the import-hygiene campaign", "summary": "**Why.** 86 of 164 modules open with a bare `import Mathlib`; 27 of them are DAG sources, so 132 of 164 modules transitively load the full 8,171-module Mathlib environment. Measured during the cold build now running: each such Lean process peaks at 6.8--7.0 GB RSS, which caps effective parallelism on a 16-core/62 GB host at about 8 jobs.\n\n**Tooling.** `scripts/min-imports.sh` runs Mathlibs `#import_bumps` (the `linter.minImports` linter) on a throwaway copy and reports the precise imports a module needs; `scripts/deumbrella.sh` rewrites the import block and re-elaborates with `lake env lean`, restoring the original on any failure so the tree is never left broken; `scripts/trim-budgets.sh` does the same for `maxHeartbeats` / `synthInstance.maxHeartbeats` / `maxRecDepth` scopes. None of them touches `.lake/build`.", "created_at": "2026-07-27T00:47:56+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/scripts/deumbrella.sh", "category": "other", "add": 69, "del": 0}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/scripts/min-imports.sh", "category": "other", "add": 63, "del": 0}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/scripts/trim-budgets.sh", "category": "other", "add": 40, "del": 0}], "lean": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 